# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tensile_*.html
Tensile_*.pdf


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transient run artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA POLICY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decision taken by the authors: the raw data is tracked and published.
# Tracked accordingly:
#   tensile_samples_data.csv, selected_all_samples*.csv   experimental strengths
#   crack_digitized_data/                14 digitized laboratory traces
#   outputs/fields/ddm_crack_sample_*.csv      14 model-derived traces
#   outputs/fields/fields_npz/           14 cached field archives (36 MB) - these
#                                        make the validation tables and figures
#                                        reproducible without the multi-hour
#                                        notebook run
#   outputs/fields/smoke_*.csv           step-wise crack diagnostics
#   (the .xlsx working spreadsheets are not published; the CSV exports above
#    are what the pipeline reads and are the published form)
# Every measurement is published in CSV form; only the working .xlsx
# spreadsheets behind them are withheld.

# Executed notebook copies are large (33 MB) and regenerable
outputs/tables/executed_notebooks/

# Solver caches. These are keyed on a hash of the specimen geometry and
# material, so they rebuild themselves when anything they depend on changes;
# committing them would only pin a stale solve.
outputs/fields/_cache_*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Present locally, not part of the published code release
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
manuscript/


# Cloud-sync scratch directories and local tool state, not project content.
.tmp.driveupload/
.tmp.drivedownload/
.backup_0809/
.claude/

# revision_log.csv is an internal working document and is NOT published.
# It was tracked until now, and a bare ignore rule would have done nothing,
# because git ignores only untracked paths. It has been untracked with
# `git rm --cached revision_log.csv`; the rule below keeps it that way and the
# file stays in the working tree.
revision_log.csv


# Excel files are not published. The two specimen workbooks are working
# documents: the replicate spreadsheet and the averaged table that
# data_mean.ipynb writes. Both are superseded for any downstream use by the
# CSV exports, which are tracked and are what the pipeline actually reads.
# rock_strength_metrics.xlsx is written by the metric export and is kept,
# because it is an output of the workflow rather than an input to it.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
*.xlsb
!rock_strength_metrics.xlsx
